</name></person-group><article-title>Mapping for prevention: GIS models for directing childhood lead poisoning prevention programs</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><year>2002</year><volume>110</volume><fpage>947</fpage><lpage>953</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12204831</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hadjichristodoulou</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Soteriades</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Kolonia</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Falagas</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Pantelopoulos</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Panagakos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mouchtouri</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Kremastinou</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Methodological aspects of a GIS-based environmental health inspection program used in the Athens 2004 Olympic and Para Olympic Games</article-title><source>BMC Public Health</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>93</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16138924</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2458-5-93</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stone</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodgers</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Urban form and thermal efficiency &#x02013; how the design of cities influences the urban heat island effect</article-title><source>J Am Plann Assoc</source><year>2001</year><volume>67</volume><fpage>186</fpage><lpage>198</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>